<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Entitlements for the containing app.

  Authority: ADR-0016 §11.2's hardening table's iOS/iPadOS row; ADR-0016 §11.4
  (the declared residual); ADR-0020 §11.3's iOS row and ST-30.

  The app needs `vpn.api` to present the consent flow (ADR-0016 §11.2's iOS
  table: "`NETunnelProviderManager` configuration and VPN-profile installation |
  App | Only the app can present the consent flow"), and it shares the keychain
  access group and the App Group with the extension because the two are one app
  identity.

  ===========================================================================
  WHAT THE SHARING COSTS, DECLARED RATHER THAN GLOSSED
  ===========================================================================

  ADR-0016 §11.4's compromised-process table, iOS/iPadOS column: an attacker in
  the APP process can "use DeviceKey as signing oracle = **Yes — declared
  residual**", because `kSecAttrAccessGroup` cannot be scoped below app identity.
  It cannot: obtain the tun descriptor, write the firewall, change routes or the
  resolver, disarm enforcement, inject code into the provider, or export the
  DeviceKey's private material — those are all OS-enforced.

  PS-24 condition 4 states the consequence in terms: PS-1's "sole holder of the
  key handle" clause is, "on HC-2 only, a declared residual rather than an
  enforceable property, tested as a declaration in P16."

  ADR-0020 ST-30's single-opener rule is likewise a DISCIPLINE here and not a
  sandbox: the app holds the App Group entitlement and MUST NOT open the vault.
  PS-24 condition 2's per-fact writer table is what makes that checkable.

  STATUS: written, not compiled and not signed.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.developer.networking.vpn.api</key>
    <array>
        <string>allow-vpn</string>
    </array>

    <key>com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension</key>
    <array>
        <string>packet-tunnel-provider</string>
    </array>

    <key>keychain-access-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)group.net.twinvpn.client</string>
    </array>

    <key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>group.net.twinvpn.client</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
